# L §2.4 (tally 2.1.3, issue #59): version items sort "by target id, ..., then keys in index order (...), with a keyless
# row first"; "At one key position the wider key comes first", and a trailing key left out covers every key there
# (L §4.6 step 3.2: "anything inside `*` or a trailing key left out"). So keys compare position by position as a list,
# and a row that leaves a key out sorts before one that states a key at that position, as the keyless row before a
# keyed one: wealth[e1] = 0 before wealth[e1, savings] and wealth[e1, shares], whatever the file's order. The rows of
# UL-09's version facts_2022 (wealth[ex22_1] = 0 beside wealth[ex22_1, savings] = 150 000), reduced. Was a crash:
# canon.cmp_comp compared a key with the span's Tie (TypeError, T's SR-2).
=== options reprint
=== m.tally
model t
  tally 2
  on 2026-12-31
  start 2026-01-01
  end 2026-12-31

source s "s"

index ex = [e1, e2]
index item = [savings, shares]
input wealth[e in ex, i in item]: int

version v
  cite s
  governs always
  known 2026-01-01
  wealth[e2, shares] = 5
  wealth[e1, shares] = 7
  wealth[e1] = 0
  wealth[e1, savings] = 150 000
